---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii4_53",
  "series": "Band II 4 (1701 - 1707)",
  "seq": 53,
  "text": "<p> [[176.11]] <b>53. BURCHARD DE VOLDER AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[176.12]] Leiden, 30. Oktober 1703. [42.54.] </b></p>\n<p> [[177.1]] Amplissimo Viro D^#'o Godefrido Guilelmo Leibnitzio S. P. B. De Volder. </p>\n<p> [[177.2]] Quo magis tua perpendo, eo minus miror te saepius scripsisse, ita tibi mente praecepta\n[[177.3]] esse omnia, ut ad quaslibet objectiones respondere promtus sis. Videor enim mihi animadvertere,\n[[177.4]] te in tua Hypothesi involvere, quidquid ex legibus Mechanicis sequi potest, adeoque\n[[177.5]] frustra ex iis contra te arma parari. Imo videor etiam mihi (an vere, tui erit judicii) quasi per\n[[177.6]] transennam viam aspicere, qua quis ad illa ita stabilienda pervenire queat. Nam si assumam,\n[[177.7]] varias in hac universitate rerum esse substantias, easque in se invicem non agere, reliqua non\n[[177.8]] difficulter videntur sequi. Etenim cum experientia doceat mutationem fieri, ea autem absque\n[[177.9]] actione et passione fieri nequeat, substantia autem altera in alteram nec agere nec ab altera pati\n[[177.10]] possit, necessum erit, ut aut cum Malebranchio Deum e machina accersamus; aut tecum\n[[177.11]] assumamus in unaquaque substantia esse quandam agendi vim, eamque omnes sui mutationes\n[[177.12]] in se continere, easque successive evolvere. Cui rei et consequens erit, cum nulla substantia\n[[177.13]] interire queat a semetipsa, nec ab alia, utpote quae in eam agere nequit, unamquamque semper\n[[177.14]] manere unam eandemque; imo in se et praeterita et praesentia, et futura tempora involvere, et\n[[177.15]] quae plura id genus in tua Hypothesi apparent <greek>parádoja</greek>. </p>\n<p> [[177.16]] Tuam equidem hypothesin Malebranchianae longe praeferrem vel eo, quod ille ad singulos\n[[177.17]] actus Deum requirat, tu vero <greek>fysikv́teron</greek>, ad primum solummodo productionis rerum actum.\n[[177.18]] Hoc tamen utrique videtur commune, quod illam aut primae <greek>ĕntelexeiṽn</greek> productionis, aut in\n[[177.19]] singulis Divinae actionis rationem relinquat obscuram admodum; Deinde et illud, quod per\n[[177.20]] leges Mechanicas, utpote quae utraque assumit, everti neutra possit. </p>\n<p> [[177.21]] Praeter quae in tua causa id me insuper male habet, quod videaris gratis assumere omnem\n[[177.22]] substantiam esse activam, cum tuam vocis substantiae definitionem ingrediatur agendi principium.\n[[177.23]] Quare, ne de voce lis sit, mihi adhucdum demonstrandum videtur primum illud, quod\n[[177.24]] inter nos quaesitum fuit, nihil posse existere, quod agendi potentiam non habeat. </p>\n<p> [[177.25]] Dein ne sic quidem satis percipio, quid id sit, quod substantiam voces. Si quid enim, nihil\n[[177.26]] certe praeter vim activam, et resistentiam percipio harum vero virium subjectum, quae tibi, ut\n[[177.27]] opinor, ipsa demum substantia est, nequaquam percipio. </p>\n<p> [[177.28]] Nunc ad litteras tuas redeo, ad quas breviter sic habe. </p>\n<p> [[177.29]] Pro causa nexus inter materiam et vim activam, quam quaesiveram, adducis omnem\n[[177.30]] substantiam esse activam, et omnem finitam esse passivam, sed hoc ipsum est <greek>tò krinómenon</greek>,\n[[177.31]] cujus demonstratio quaerebatur. Nec satis capio cur in substantia passivam potentiam requiras.\n[[177.32]] Nam cum illa a nulla pati possit alia, haec resistentia nulli rei inserviet, quam ut suae vi activae\n[[177.33]] resistat. </p>\n<p> [[177.34]] Corpora <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> aequalia, ejusdem figurae et motus nullam intrinsecam habent diversitatem;\n[[177.35]] Id tamen verum est dari causam, cur corpus <i>A</i> hunc potius locum occupet, quam illum; sed\n[[177.36]] illa non tam dependet ex natura ipsius corporis <i>A</i> intrinseca, quam ex systemate totius universi.\n[[177.37]] Ex quo sequitur, ut dato tempore corpus <i>A</i> hunc locum occupet, <i>B</i> illum, imo ex quo praeterea\n[[178.1]] sequuntur omnia loca, quae illa corpora seorsim porro occupatura sint. Quod autem intrinsecam\n[[178.2]] hic videris differentiam ponere, id non tam rerum naturae, quam tuae hypothesi deberi mihi\n[[178.3]] persuadeo. </p>\n<p> [[178.4]] Fateor nullam in corporibus quocunque modo mutatis differentiam fore, si omnes diversae\n[[178.5]] earum vires, aut diversa virium effecta tollantur. Sed si illae vires quas derivatas vocas in illis\n[[178.6]] ponantur, vel secundum Malebranchianam hypothesin effecta ipsarum virium undecunque\n[[178.7]] etiam accersita mihi eadem quae nunc secutura videntur Phaenomena. </p>\n<p> [[178.8]] Quod addis, <i>pro entibus realibus et substantiis habendis careri non posse veris unitatibus</i>,\n[[178.9]] ut et, <i>si nullum vere unum adest</i>, <i>omnis vera res erit sublata</i>; aut non intelligo, aut ex hypothesi\n[[178.10]] tua assumitur. </p>\n<p> [[178.11]] Ex eodem, opinor, fundamento negas fieri posse, ut vires derivatae solae corporibus\n[[178.12]] adsint. Veruntamen si statuamus massam corpoream instructam certa quadam vi motus ex\n[[178.13]] massa et velocitate deducendam, habituri equidem sumus eadem quae nunc Phaenomena. Nec\n[[178.14]] quicquam apparet deduci posse ex viribus quae primitivae et stabiles in diversis massae insint\n[[178.15]] partibus nisi ut secundum te particulares substantiae vocari queant, cum forte totum hoc\n[[178.16]] universum corporeum sit una tantum substantia. </p>\n<p> [[178.17]] Quod in prioribus meis dixeram, unumquodque corpus ab alio corpore affici, id non ex\n[[178.18]] entelechiis sed ex viribus derivatis deduxeram. Rem simplicem mutari posse nullus dubito, sed\n[[178.19]] a se mutari posse, non existimo. Semper enim mihi persuasi, quidquid ex natura rei sequitur, id\n[[178.20]] rei semper adesse invariato modo, certe quamdiu manet eadem natura rei, nec ab ea tolli posse,\n[[178.21]] cum inter id ipsum, et naturam rei nexus sit necessarius; Mutationem ergo, quae accidit\n[[178.22]] manente eadem rei natura, necessario deberi causae externae. Dicis quidem <i>substantiae finitae\n[[178.23]] essentialem esse internam tendentiam ad mutationem</i>. Verum hoc ipsum illud est, quod\n[[178.24]] demonstrationem exigit, et quod allato modo ratiocinio, nisi fallor, evertitur. Vale. </p>\n<p> [[178.25]] Lugd. Batav. a. d. XXX Octobris MDCCIII </p>\n",
  "number": "53.",
  "title": "BURCHARD DE VOLDER AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Leiden, 30. Oktober 1703. [42.54.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:53. BURCHARD DE VOLDER AN LEIBNIZ Leiden, 30. Oktober 1703. [42.54.] Amplissimo Viro D^#'o Godefrido Guilelmo Leibnitzio S. P. B. De Volder. Quo magis tua perpendo, eo minus miror te saepius scripsisse, ita tibi mente praecepta esse omnia, ut ad quaslibet objectiones respondere promtus sis. Videor e...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>